NOTICE — this application's third-party components and behaviour references
==========================================================================

This file is the bundle-level attribution the programme asks every card to keep current
(`docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` §3 rule 4). The full verification record — pinned refs, commit
SHAs, how each licence was checked — is `docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`; this is its summary.

1. Code that ships inside the app
---------------------------------

  GRDB.swift — MIT — https://github.com/groue/GRDB.swift
  Resolved by SwiftPM (7.11.1, `upToNextMajorVersion` from 7.0.0) and linked into the app and the
  test bundle. No GRDB source is vendored into this repository; the MIT licence text is carried by
  the package itself, as SwiftPM requires.

  No other third-party library, icon font, emoji sprite or bundled asset is part of the app.
  Icons are SF Symbols. The bundled emoji shortcode table (`Mattermost/Resources/emoji.json`) is
  generated by this repository's own script from Unicode data, not copied from an upstream client.

2. Behaviour references — no source copied
------------------------------------------

  mattermost/mattermost-mobile @ v2.45.0 (Apache-2.0) and the Mattermost web app in
  mattermost/mattermost (webapp/ — Apache-2.0) are read to establish *behaviour*: request shapes,
  ordering and decision rules, screen anatomy, copy re-worded in this repository's own files.
  No source file, in whole or in part, is copied or transpiled into this repository, and the Swift
  code is written against the public REST v4 / WebSocket v4 contract
  (https://api.mattermost.com). Per-file headers name the upstream path each file derives from
  (`docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` §3).

  The Mattermost *server* (AGPL-3.0 / commercial) is never ported: this app contains no server
  code and no AGPL licence text, and reaches the server only over its public HTTP/WebSocket APIs.

